{
  "_doc": "PHASE 0 ONLY of the co-residency campaign declared in records/headers/2026-08-22-coresidency-matrix.json (arms[0]). Every (rig, engine, model) loaded ALONE, recording the measured resident footprint in the shape its engine can state (ADR-0040). No pairs, no co-residency, no throughput, no latency, no concurrency ramps.",
  "_intent_header": "records/headers/2026-08-22-coresidency-matrix.json",
  "_ramp_off": "collect.concurrency is false, so run.py:506's gate (collect.concurrency AND the entry's concurrency.measure) is never satisfied and every ramp is skipped. A cell is a load plus reads. No entry declares `concurrency` at all, so no entry claims a measurement this run does not take.",
  "_roster_provenance": "Enumerated LIVE on 2026-08-23: ollama /api/tags on each rig, and ~/.cache/huggingface/hub on each rig for AWQ checkpoints. srv1 = 5 ollama + 3 AWQ; srv2 = 13 ollama + 4 AWQ; 25 cells. srv1's models--nvidia--NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-4B-FP8 is excluded twice over: srv1 is compute capability 7.5 and FP8 needs 8.9, and that cache entry holds no snapshot (12K, no config.json).",
  "_ordering": "Within each host the engines ALTERNATE where both are present. run.py's exclusion loop releases only the OTHER backends, so a vLLM cell following a vLLM cell would read its `card before` while the previous vLLM server still held the card (vllm._start releases its own server later, inside the claim). Alternating keeps every recorded before-reading a reading of an empty card. Largest models last, so a cheap cell is never lost behind an expensive one.",
  "_vllm_declaration": "ONE serving geometry across the whole arm - max_model_len 8192, max_num_seqs 8 - with kv_cache_memory_bytes derived per model as max_num_seqs * max_model_len * bytes_per_token (ADR-0039; never gpu_memory_utilization, which is the header's second void_if). bytes_per_token = num_hidden_layers * num_key_value_heads * head_dim * 2 (K and V) * 2 (fp16), read off each checkpoint's own config.json on the rig. A declaration that does not fit the card is a REFUSAL and a row, not a cell to be re-tuned until it loads.",
  "_expect_note": "ollama entries pin model_sha256, read off each rig's own /api/tags on 2026-08-23. vLLM entries pin nothing: weights_sha256 is computed and recorded by the claim either way, and a pin whose value was measured on the other rig would cost a footprint reading to test an identity this phase is not asking about.",
